So I think what is important here is what kind of "legal trouble" you are actually looking for. Are you trying to stay out of court and within the bounds of the law? What kind of countries are you looking to stay under the watchful eye of? This is an important thing because there are some countries that have made it explicitly illegal to advocate hate against groups, including Jews. Dec 14, 2018 at 14:34
@CortAmmon you need to elaborate. Are you sure that there is something like that which would stop them from posting anti-Semitic content without getting into any legal trouble? Dec 14, 2018 at 16:04
@Nelson: The United States does not criminalize hate speech. Nor does Germany for that matter. So this answer, by far, should be the correct answer. You can say whatever you want. The rest of the answer was just that there are some places that criminalize hate speech, which is why it is important to define your environment before recommending how to do it in such a way that you avoid trouble. You would be safer here in the US, but some other countries could make it much more difficult. Dec 14, 2018
